From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000062 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Petr Parkan Janda <petronijus@bastla.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: omap4-steelhead: run the SGX from DPLL_PER like stock

On the 4460 mainline leaves the SGX functional-clock mux on its reset
parent, dpll_core_m7x2_ck, so the GPU would run at 266.67 MHz (live on
6.18.48-r20: l3-gfx-clkctrl:0000:24 <- dpll_core_m7x2_ck 266666667).
Stock reparents gpu_fck to dpll_per_m7x2_ck in
omap4_steelhead_display_init() (vmlinux.bin @0xc0075f40), and all three
stock 446x GPU OPPs (153.6/307.2/384 MHz) are dividers of DPLL_PER.
Mainline carries the same block only in omap443x.dtsi.

Assign the parent and stock's OPP100 rate, 307.2 MHz, on the ti-sysc
target module (the binding forbids clocks on gpu@0). It needs VDD_CORE
>= 1.127 V; the stock x-loader programs VCORE1 to 1.139 V on every boot.
384 MHz needs 1.25 V and mainline cannot scale VDD_CORE, so it is not
used. dpll_per_m7x2_ck has no ti,set-rate-parent and already runs at
307.2 MHz, so no other DPLL_PER output moves (M3 -> TAS5713 MCLK
included). ti-sysc enables the clock only briefly at probe for the
revision read; it runs only once a GPU driver binds.

Precondition: 307.2 MHz relies on the x-loader's VCORE1 setpoint and
on CORE never entering RET (0055/0057 keep it out), so the TWL6030
never drops VCORE1 to its sleep value. Enabling CORE RET, or binding a
GPU driver before the kernel sends the CORE ON voltage itself, voids it.

Audited against stock: docs/gpu-sgx540/stock-ground-truth.md §4,
docs/gpu-sgx540/power-clocks-pm.md Addendum §7.

Signed-off-by: Petr Parkan Janda <petronijus@bastla.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-steelhead.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-steelhead.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-steelhead.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-steelhead.dts
@@ -908,6 +908,31 @@
 };
 
 /*
+ * GPU (PowerVR SGX540 rev 1.2.0): run the functional clock from DPLL_PER M7,
+ * as stock does. Stock omap4_steelhead_display_init() calls
+ * clk_set_parent(gpu_fck, dpll_per_m7x2_ck), and every stock 446x GPU OPP
+ * (153.6 / 307.2 / 384 MHz at VDD_CORE 962 / 1127 / 1250 mV) is a divider of
+ * DPLL_PER x2 = 1536 MHz. Mainline does this only for the 4430
+ * (omap443x.dtsi, 307.2 MHz, "like droid4 stock"); omap4460.dtsi has no such
+ * block, so without it the SGX runs from dpll_core_m7x2_ck at 266.67 MHz.
+ *
+ * 307.2 MHz is stock OPP100 and needs VDD_CORE >= 1.127 V; the x-loader sets
+ * VCORE1 to 1.139 V on every boot. Mainline has no VDD_CORE scaling, so
+ * 384 MHz (OPP-OV, 1.25 V) is deliberately not used. dpll_per_m7x2_ck has no
+ * ti,set-rate-parent, so the rate request cannot move DPLL_PER or its other
+ * outputs. The img,powervr-sgx binding forbids clocks on the gpu@0 child for
+ * ti,omap4430-gpu, so the assignment sits on the ti-sysc target module.
+ * Applied when ti-sysc probes the module; the clock is enabled only briefly
+ * for the ti-sysc revision read at probe and runs only once a GPU driver binds.
+ */
+&sgx_module {
+	assigned-clocks = <&l3_gfx_clkctrl OMAP4_GPU_CLKCTRL 24>,
+			  <&dpll_per_m7x2_ck>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <0>, <307200000>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <&dpll_per_m7x2_ck>;
+};
+
+/*
  * MPU cpufreq: cpu-supply = the VC-bridge regulator (drives the TPS62361 via the
  * Voltage Controller, VP force-update). OPP table = OPP50/100/Turbo/Nitro
  * (350 / 700 / 920 / 1200 MHz); the cpu-supply scales VDD_MPU 1025..1380 mV with
